A||N||6||FieroFanaticus2||What Rivets will Work for this??||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||07-07-2001||12:49 PM||||Ok, since I can't find a reasonably prices monobolt setter for installing new monobolts for the rocker panel when I put on the side scoops, what other type of rivets will work?<BR>Maybe I can use 1/4 inch aluminum and just put some washers on the front and back?<BR>Anybody who has put side scoops on, what did you use?  Please help!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||07-07-2001||01:39 PM||||I used rivnuts with screws and countersunk washers.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||07-07-2001||04:10 PM||||I use Cherry Klamp-tite 1/4" aluminum rivets. They have three wings that spread out on the underside when you pull them. I get them from J.O King in Tampa, 813-885-4419. Or you can call Cherry at 714-545-5511 to find a distributor in your area.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_Freak||07-07-2001||04:50 PM||||   I bought a rivet gun from Harbor Frieght.  It has a bunch of the correct size rivets with it and it's only like $17.. I think.  <P>Here it is... <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=41291" TARGET=_blank>http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=41291</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||14
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||07-07-2001||05:18 PM||||Well I have a rivet gun but it won't set monobolts.  I think I'm going to try calling that cherry place and see if a regular rivet gun can set those, if not I'll just use some nuts and bolts, maybe put some washers on there too.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||07-07-2001||06:10 PM||||Depending on how permanent you want them.....<P>You can use "screw rivits" to anchor them along the door frame. You can get these at allot of parts stores. The same ones I use for the door skins should work for these. get the motor mite part number from my cave article. If those are wrong then I'm sure there is one that will work.<P>To set these you just shove on the "screw" with a philips head driver. They are black plastic and will look reasonably stock.<P>Nice thing is if you later move the panel to another car you can unscrew the centers to get the panel off. (Which is the big reason I like them for the door skins. I've had mine off at least twice now for one reason or another.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||PJ||07-07-2001||09:40 PM||||You can set the Cherry Klamp-tites with a regular ¼" rivet gun. They come structural or non-structural in various grip lengths. I had to buy 200 of 'em to meet a minimum order requirement. I think they were .12¢ ea. I gave a handful of them to the body shop a few doors down and they were back a week later wanting to know where I got them from.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
